-- A STRING-sorted PARAMETER on a derived predicate that Blawx never declares.
--
-- This is the sibling of `string-field.l4`, and it exists because the first cut
-- of the STRING refusal did not catch it. The refusal lives in
-- `blawxValueType` (L4.Blawx.Lower), but that function is only reached from the
-- two arms of `classifyPred` that build a DECLARATION BLOCK: the attribute arm
-- and the arity-3-and-up relationship arm. A predicate of total arity 2 that is
-- not attribute-shaped falls through to `PCUndeclared` — rules only, no block —
-- and so was never asked what its parameters were sorted at.
--
-- Measured on this module before the fix (2026-09-02): `l4 blawx` exited 0 and
-- wrote an s(CASP) dump containing
--
--     according_to(sec_1_section,throws_named,P,S) :- player(P), S = zebra.
--
-- with no `blawx_attribute` or `blawx_relationship` line for `throws_named` at
-- all — and it re-saved clean through Blawx's own generator. Raising the same
-- predicate to total arity 3 was refused, which is what kept the hole out of
-- sight. `classifyPred` now runs a STRING pre-pass over the whole signature
-- before classifying, so all three positions — field, parameter, result — give
-- the same named diagnostic:
--
--   in `throws named`: STRING-sorted field or argument (Blawx): `throws named`
--   has a STRING-sorted field, parameter or result, and Blawx's ontology has no
--   string attribute type — …
--
-- The remedy is the one `string-field.l4` spells out: an enum for a fixed
-- vocabulary, a category for identity. String LITERALS in a rule body are still
-- fine — it is the sort in the signature that has nowhere to go
-- (BLAWX-EXPORT-SPEC §4.7).

§ `String-typed parameter`

DECLARE Sign IS ONE OF Rock, Paper, Scissors

DECLARE Player HAS
    throws IS A Sign

@export 1. A player throws under a given name.
GIVEN p IS A Player
      s IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `throws named` p s IF s EQUALS "zebra"
